  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lactose is composed of a molecule of galactose joined to a molecule of glucose by a &beta;-1,4-glycosidic linkage. It is a reducing sugar that is found in milk.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0125_0e2467cb516f.png\" style=\"width: 430px; height: 187px;\" /></p><p>In lactose linkage is formed between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> of galactose and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> of glucose.</p>"
